{"content":"## Merlin

Merlin begins the journey with a focus on building a strong aerobic base. In the early weeks, runners should prioritize consistent, easy-paced runs to condition the heart and lungs while allowing the body to adapt to the increased load. Rest days are just as important as training days at this stage, giving muscles time to repair and strengthen. Cross-training activities like cycling or swimming can complement running without adding undue stress.
